-- Two --always properties whose counterexamples pass through `taken now`, a
-- constant that reads a ledger, in an imported file (taken.l4). On the skip
-- path it is first asked by `look`, after `taken` is committed, and is TRUE;
-- on the peek path it is asked by `go`, before, and is FALSE. Each
-- counterexample is replayed before it is printed, and each replay has its
-- own copy of the constant, as the exploration's do. On a build whose
-- counterexample replay shared one copy, with the clock fixed, the second
-- property's replay read the first one's answer and its counterexample did
-- not replay, in either order (review of smucclaw/l4-ide#1107).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT taken

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Bob
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF peek, skip
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF
    go HAS mode IS A Mode
    look

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`after` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY look
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `seen` IS `taken now` HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`start` MEANS
    PARTY Bob
    MAY go m
    WITHIN 10
    HENCE COMMIT `taken` IS (IF m EQUALS peek THEN NOT `taken now` ELSE TRUE) HENCE `after`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVEN seen IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`nothing seen` seen MEANS NOT (fromMaybe FALSE seen)

GIVEN seen IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`never seen false` seen MEANS fromMaybe TRUE seen
